 "notes": "'method' = Ours-lowrate: lambda_e=0.004 for real-scene datasets (= default lmbda in official run_shell_mip360/tnt/db.py), lambda_e=0.002 for synthetic_nerf. 'method_lambda_<l>' records each of the five lambda_e settings (0.004,0.003,0.002,0.001,0.0005) separately. Main Table 1 mapping (verified against supp. averages): real-scene datasets (mipnerf360/tandt/db/bungeenerf) Ours-lowrate = lambda 0.004, Ours-highrate = lambda 0.001; Synthetic-NeRF Ours-lowrate = lambda 0.002, Ours-highrate = lambda 0.0005. size_mb = total compressed bitstream in MiB (bits/(8*1024*1024)): anchors(16-bit) + AE-coded feat/scaling/offsets + AE-coded binary hash grid + AE-coded masks + MLPs(fp32). baseline_3dgs and baseline_scaffold_gs are the per-scene rows from HAC's supplementary (these 3DGS numbers are NOT the 3DGS paper's: e.g. Mip-NeRF360 avg 27.49 vs 27.21, T&T 23.69 vs 23.14 in tools/reference_results.json; their protocol is UNVERIFIED: HAC only says it follows Scaffold-GS; they are likely copied from the Scaffold-GS paper (Scaffold-GS sizes are rounded integers) and it is an unverified assumption that they share HAC's 1.6K-width protocol; judge fidelity against HAC's own rows and our own baselines on identical images). Mip-NeRF360 is evaluated on all 9 scenes; the paper table spells 'flower' -> key 'flowers'. Eval resolution in official code: Mip-NeRF360 loads full-res 'images' and auto-downscales to width 1600 (-r -1), NOT images_4/images_2; T&T and DB at native resolution of the 3DGS tandt_db release. llffhold=8 test split, black background, LPIPS-VGG (lpipsPyTorch). Mip-NeRF360 lambda 0.0005 reported PSNR average 27.83 vs mean of per-scene 27.837 (rounding only). Table labels follow the PDF text: supp. Table B Synthetic-NeRF, C Mip-NeRF360, D T&T, E DeepBlending, F BungeeNeRF, G 3DGS, H Scaffold-GS (LaTeX labels in parentheses).",
